{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 400}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 107, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e0 absent, e3 is often the only live path to the output, so deleting it collapses the cell (e.g., #8, #32, #360)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When e0 is none, node 2 depends solely on e1, so removing e1 kills the node-2 branch (e.g., #38, #365, #400)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If e1 is none, e0 feeds both intermediate nodes, so removing it leaves only the direct e3 path (e.g., #75, #114, #144)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool on the direct input-output edge with a conv adds substantial capacity (e.g., #162, #175, #183)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping avg_pool for a learnable conv on edge 3 gives large gains (e.g., #92, #182, #337)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on the direct path beats pooling there, whereas replacing a conv with skip loses capacity (e.g., #59, #88, #309)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning a learnable conv on the direct edge into pooling strongly hurts (e.g., #212, #186, #248)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a pool where there was no edge opens a new path, while replacing a conv with pool removes capacity (e.g., #70, #54, #247)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why"